# XSH ctermid()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The test process is never assumed to have a controlling terminal. The one
# assertion that needs a controlling terminal makes a session of its own and
# a pseudo-terminal (XSI) to be it.
#
# "when BASE|XSI": the requirements are Base; XSI is named only so that the
# driver builds these tests with the XSI feature macro (the pseudo-terminal
# set-up needs it). They run wherever they build, and a set-up that is not
# available is UNRESOLVED.

assertion  XSH.ctermid.001
anchor     functions/ctermid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       ctermid(buf) with a buffer of L_ctermid bytes returns buf,
           leaves a null-terminated string within those L_ctermid bytes,
           and does not write the guard bytes after them.
test       t/001-buffer.c

assertion  XSH.ctermid.002
anchor     functions/ctermid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       L_ctermid is defined by <stdio.h> and is greater than 0.
test       t/002-l_ctermid.c

assertion  XSH.ctermid.003
anchor     functions/ctermid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       ctermid(NULL) returns a non-null pointer to a null-terminated
           string (empty if the pathname cannot be determined).
note       See Q-84: RATIONALE calls the result undefined, RETURN VALUE
           defines it; the test follows RETURN VALUE. Only one call is
           made and the string is only read.
test       t/003-null-arg.c

assertion  XSH.ctermid.004
anchor     functions/ctermid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap11.html#11.1.3
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       In a session leader that has a pseudo-terminal as its
           controlling terminal, if ctermid() returns a non-empty string
           and opening it succeeds, the descriptor is the controlling
           terminal: tcgetpgrp() on it returns the process group of the
           session leader (the foreground group a new controlling terminal
           starts with). An empty string or a failed open (access is not
           guaranteed) is NOTINUSE.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. How a
           session leader acquires a controlling terminal is
           implementation-defined (XBD 11.1.3); UNRESOLVED if opening the
           subsidiary device without O_NOCTTY does not make it the
           controlling terminal.
test       t/004-names-ctty.c
